    "field": "Statistical physics of the atmosphere",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the challenge of describing the complex transition to intense atmospheric precipitation by applying the theoretical framework of critical phenomena, proposing that this transition behaves as a continuous phase transition with water vapor acting as the key tuning parameter.",
    "method": "We propose analyzing satellite observations of atmospheric water vapor and precipitation using the theoretical framework of critical phenomena to characterize the onset of intense convection as a continuous phase transition exhibiting self-organized criticality.",
    "task": "The task is to demonstrate, using satellite data, that the transition to intense atmospheric precipitation behaves as a non-equilibrium continuous phase transition, where a critical value of water vapour acts as a tuning parameter, consistent with the theory of self-organized criticality.",
